meta {
  name: Ask (grounded, SSE)
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/chat
  body: json
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: text/event-stream
}

body:json {
  {
    "message": "{{askQuestion}}",
    "session_id": "{{sessionId}}"
  }
}

docs {
  Ask a grounded, cited question (uses the `askQuestion` variable). Streams Server-Sent Events:
  thinking / delta / tool_call / tool_result / sources / candidates / answer / done. Answers only from
  learned memory, or says it hasn't learned that yet. `session_id` and `project` are optional.

  `tool_call` and `tool_result` carry JSON in `data` — `{id, name, args}` and
  `{id, name, ok, summary, chars}` — paired by `id` and interleaved with `thinking` in the
  real order the run happened, so a client can render it as a step-by-step trace. `summary`
  is a bounded preview; `chars` is the true size of the output the model received.

  `sources` carries `[{label, uri, link?, kind?, score?, snippet}]` — the citable refs a tool
  result newly introduced, additive across the turn. It is what lets a citation of a readable
  title ("Caffeine - Team Charter") resolve to the page it came from and render as a link.
  `uri` is IDENTITY and is not always browsable (a cloned repo file is `<clone-url>::<path>`);
  `link` is where the citation should open, and is absent when there is no web address —
  link on `link`, never on `uri`.
}
